#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:7
msgid "Hermes Telegram Lock Conflict Fix"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:9
msgid "Problem"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:10
msgid "Multiple Hermes gateway agents on the same machine produce lock conflicts:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:11
msgid ""
"\"Another local Hermes gateway is already using this Telegram bot token "
"(PID XXXXX)\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:12
msgid "\"Telegram status fatal\" despite valid bot tokens"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:13
msgid "WhatsApp also affected with same pattern"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:15
msgid "Root Causes (5 found)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:17
msgid "1. Systemd service hardcodes TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:18
msgid ""
"The default agent's systemd unit (`/etc/systemd/system/hermes-"
"gateway.service`) has:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:22
msgid ""
"This env var **overrides** config.yaml's "
"`platforms.telegram.enabled=false`. The gateway reads env first, always "
"connects to Telegram, and steals the lock from cmd agents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:24
msgid "2. Multiple concurrent gateway processes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:25
msgid ""
"Every new session turn can spawn `hermes gateway run`, stacking processes"
" that all try to poll the same bot token. Telegram only allows one "
"polling connection per token."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:27
msgid "3. Stale lock files at ~/.local/state/hermes/gateway-locks/"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:28
msgid "Lock files persist after gateway crashes. They reference dead PIDs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:30
msgid "4. Stale gateway_state.json"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:31
msgid "Contains old PIDs and fatal error states that mislead new agents."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:33
msgid "5. gateway-run.sh sources same gateway.env for all agents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:34
msgid "All agents inherit same TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN from default gateway.env."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:36
msgid "Fix Procedure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:38
msgid "Step 1: Remove TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN from default systemd service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:44
msgid "Step 2: Disable telegram on default agent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:60
msgid "Step 3: Kill ALL gateways and clean state"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:73
msgid "Step 4: Restart services"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:80
msgid "Verification"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:99
msgid "Architecture Reference"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:100
msgid ""
"Default agent: ~/.hermes/ (should NOT poll Telegram - cmd agents handle "
"it)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:101
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Cmd agents: ~/hermes_cmd_agent{1-4}/ (each has unique Telegram bot token)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:102
msgid "Each cmd agent needs its own gateway-run.sh sourcing its own .env"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:103
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Lock files: ~/.local/state/hermes/gateway-locks/telegram-bot-"
"token-{hash}.lock"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:105
msgid "Pitfalls"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:106
msgid ""
"Setting `enabled: false` in config.yaml does NOT work if "
"TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN is in the systemd service env or gateway.env"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:107
msgid ""
"The gateway reads platform config via `PlatformConfig` which has "
"`get_env_value()` override for TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:108
msgid "Always use `sudo sed` to edit systemd files (not python without sudo)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/hermes-telegram-fix_SKILL.md:109
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Lock files use `{scope}-{identity_hash}.lock` naming - check actual hash "
"matches"
msgstr ""

